# NuGet package

Before changing package metadata, packing, or publishing, read [`.cursor/skills/nuget-package/SKILL.md`](../skills/nuget-package/SKILL.md). The guide is [package authoring best practices](https://learn.microsoft.com/nuget/create-packages/package-authoring-best-practices).

## Required

- Pack `src/Txfio/Txfio.csproj` with `dotnet pack`. Tests and stress stay `IsPackable` false
- `PackageId` `Txfio`. SemVer in `VersionPrefix` (`CONTRIBUTING.md`). Do not add a prerelease label unless the issue says the release is a preview
- `Description`, `Authors` (`YUKIKEDA`, the name on `LICENSE`), `Copyright` (the same line as `LICENSE`), `PackageLicenseExpression` `MIT`
- `PackageProjectUrl`, `RepositoryUrl`, `RepositoryType` `git`, Source Link, and a symbol package (`snupkg`)
- `PackageTags` use semicolons. `PackageReadmeFile` is `README.md`. Update `PackageReleaseNotes` (a short summary that starts with the version and links to `CHANGELOG.md`) and the undated `CHANGELOG.md` section in the same change as `VersionPrefix`
- Do not set `LicenseUrl` or `IconUrl`. Do not add `PackageIcon` unless a 128×128 transparent PNG is already in the repo

## Publish

- One package, `Txfio`. The packed readme is English `README.md` only
- The publish-ready install line is `dotnet add package Txfio`. Do not say the package is already listed on nuget.org until that push has succeeded
- A version is published only by the `Release` workflow (`.github/workflows/release.yml`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` "Releasing"). It tags the commit, pushes to nuget.org through Trusted Publishing, and creates the GitHub Release. Agents do not run it, and do not create the tag, the Release, or a nuget.org push by hand. Ready means a human runs `Release` and no other step is left
- Before calling a release ready, the documentation review in `CONTRIBUTING.md` "Releasing" is done and recorded on the release preparation pull request. Checking only the workflow and the repository settings is not "ready". When telling the user about a release, first say what was checked and what was not
- A local pack for checking passes `ContinuousIntegrationBuild`, as the workflow does. A pack without it leaves the local source path in the DLL and the PDB. Outputs are `src/Txfio/bin/Release/Txfio.<version>.nupkg` and `.snupkg`; `.github/scripts/release-check-package.sh` checks them:

```text
dotnet pack src/Txfio/Txfio.csproj -c Release -p:ContinuousIntegrationBuild=true
```

- A published version cannot be replaced
